---
import '../design/design-aids.css';
import SketchSheet from '../design/SketchSheet.astro';
---
<concurrent-schedule class="lab design-aid design-lab" aria-labelledby="concurrent-schedule-title">
  <div class="lab-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Interactive experiment</span></div>
  <h3 id="concurrent-schedule-title">Two requests, one available mug</h3>
  <div class="lab-introduction"><p>Requests A and B each want one P7 mug. A reaches the stock row first. Compare an ordinary read followed by an application-computed write, a conditional update, and a locking read. All three put stock and order changes inside transactions.</p><p class="try-this">Advance the unsafe attempt to its end, then change the method. Finally let A roll back: a waiting buyer must get a different answer when the first reservation is abandoned.</p></div>
  <div class="lab-controls" data-controls>
    <p class="lab-area-label">Controls</p>
    <div class="control-line"><label for="concurrent-method">Method</label><select id="concurrent-method" data-method><option value="unsafe">Read, decide, then write</option><option value="guard">Conditional update</option><option value="lock">Lock, read, then decide</option></select></div>
    <div class="control-line"><label for="concurrent-ending">A’s ending</label><select id="concurrent-ending" data-ending><option value="commit">Commit its purchase</option><option value="rollback">Roll back its purchase</option></select></div>
    <div class="control-line"><button type="button" data-back>Previous step</button><button type="button" data-next>Next step</button><button type="button" data-reset>Start again</button></div>
  </div>
  <div class="lab-output paper-surface">
    <p class="lab-area-label">Result <span data-step>Completed unsafe attempt</span></p>
    <div class="shared"><span>Committed P7 availability</span><strong data-stock>0</strong><span>Committed purchases for this mug</span><strong data-orders>2</strong></div>
    <div class="buyers">
      <SketchSheet tone="blue"><h4>Request A · O14</h4><p data-a>A committed one purchase.</p></SketchSheet>
      <SketchSheet tone="amber"><h4>Request B · O15</h4><p data-b>B also committed, using its earlier decision.</p></SketchSheet>
    </div>
    <p class="event" data-event role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">Both requests read 1 and decided to write 0. The final stock count is non-negative, but two purchases have claimed the one mug.</p>
  </div>
  <details class="model-note"><summary>What this experiment models</summary><p>This fixed schedule models two one-mug purchases in PostgreSQL Read Committed. The counters show committed records; the request panels describe unfinished changes. A row lock is held until the owning transaction ends. A stock update and its order commit together. The conditional branch and locking branch create an order only after obtaining stock. This is a documentation-based teaching model, not two live database connections or a performance measurement.</p></details>
  <noscript><p>The completed unsafe attempt appears above. With a conditional update or a locking read, B waits for A. If A commits, B finds no stock and creates no purchase. If A rolls back, B can reserve the mug. With all three methods, A’s rollback followed by B’s commit leaves one purchase and stock zero.</p></noscript>
</concurrent-schedule>
<script>
  class ConcurrentSchedule extends HTMLElement {
    connectedCallback() {
      if (this.dataset.ready) return;
      const method = this.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-method]')!;
      const ending = this.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-ending]')!;
      const back = this.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-back]')!;
      const next = this.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-next]')!;
      let step = 0;
      const set = (key:string, value:string|number) => { this.querySelector(`[data-${key}]`)!.textContent = String(value); };
      const render = () => {
        const unsafe = method.value === 'unsafe';
        const guard = method.value === 'guard';
        const commits = ending.value === 'commit';
        const bBuys = unsafe || !commits;
        const states = [
          ['Transaction begun; no stock read yet.', 'Transaction begun; no stock read yet.', 'One mug is available. Neither request has a reservation.'],
          [unsafe ? 'Read 1; computed a future stock value of 0.' : guard ? 'Conditional update changed 1 to 0; holds the row lock.' : 'Locked the row and read 1; holds the row lock.', 'Has not reached the stock row yet.', unsafe ? 'A’s ordinary read has not reserved the mug.' : guard ? 'A has an unfinished stock reduction. Other readers still see committed availability 1.' : 'A can now decide while a competing updater waits. The lock itself has not reduced stock.'],
          [unsafe ? 'Still plans to write 0.' : 'Holds the stock row lock.', unsafe ? 'Also read 1; also computed 0.' : guard ? 'Conditional update waits for A’s transaction to end.' : 'Locking read waits; has not returned a stock value.', unsafe ? 'Two application decisions now depend on the same available mug.' : 'B has no result yet. Waiting is neither success nor a sold-out answer.'],
          ['Has pending stock 0 and purchase O14; holds the row lock.', unsafe ? 'Submitted its planned write of 0; now waits for A.' : guard ? 'Still waiting to evaluate the update against the row it can change.' : 'Still waiting to lock and read the row.', 'A has completed its local changes but has not ended the transaction. Its purchase is not committed.'],
          [commits ? 'Committed O14 and stock 0; released its lock.' : 'Rolled back O14 and its stock change; released its lock.', unsafe ? 'Writes its previously chosen 0; prepares O15.' : commits ? guard ? 'Rechecked available >= 1 against 0; changed no row.' : 'Locked and read the updated 0; declines the purchase.' : guard ? 'Rechecked available >= 1 against 1; changed it to 0 and prepares O15.' : 'Locked and read 1; reserves the mug and prepares O15.', unsafe ? 'The write still uses the old decision, regardless of A’s outcome.' : commits ? 'A’s purchase used the mug. B’s decision now reflects that completed change.' : 'A abandoned its reservation. B can reserve the mug once A’s lock is released.'],
          [commits ? 'O14 committed.' : 'O14 absent: A rolled back.', bBuys ? 'O15 committed.' : 'No O15: B rolled back without reserving stock.', unsafe && commits ? 'Two committed purchases for one mug. Stock is 0, so a non-negative constraint does not reveal the overselling.' : 'One committed purchase for the one mug. Stock is 0.']
        ];
        const state = states[step];
        set('step', `Step ${step} of 5`);
        set('stock', step === 5 ? 0 : step >= 4 && commits ? 0 : 1);
        set('orders', step === 5 ? Number(commits) + Number(bBuys) : step >= 4 && commits ? 1 : 0);
        set('a', state[0]); set('b', state[1]); set('event', state[2]);
        back.disabled = step === 0; next.disabled = step === 5;
      };
      back.addEventListener('click', () => { step = Math.max(0, step-1); render(); });
      next.addEventListener('click', () => { step = Math.min(5, step+1); render(); });
      this.querySelector('[data-reset]')!.addEventListener('click', () => { step = 0; render(); });
      method.addEventListener('change', () => { step = 0; render(); });
      ending.addEventListener('change', () => { step = 0; render(); });
      render(); this.dataset.ready = 'true';
    }
  }
  if (!customElements.get('concurrent-schedule')) customElements.define('concurrent-schedule', ConcurrentSchedule);
</script>
<style>
  .shared { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto; gap:.65rem 1rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule); padding-bottom:1rem; margin-bottom:1.2rem; font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); }
  .shared strong { font:500 1.3rem/1.2 var(--font-mono); }
  .buyers { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:1rem; }
  .buyers p { font:.85rem/1.65 var(--font-sans); margin:.6rem 0 0; }
  .event { border-left:2px solid var(--teal); padding-left:.9rem; font:.875rem/1.7 var(--font-sans); margin:1.3rem 0 .3rem; }
  @media(max-width:550px) { .buyers { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
</style>
